Trails — Knowledge to learn and use (@trails: 0, is #chapter, #contains "../ergon/Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1", #contains "../scholazein/Scholazein.lingua#r_E8E2D1B2D2994E0AD5F5D002D6", #contains "../ascholia/Ascholia.lingua#r_C13F57992B4DED1C03FB1AF28D", #contains "Lince-trails.lingua#r_5CC329E69581876107C84531CE", #contains "../pathways/First-connected-pathways.lingua#r_3RYVEGQ60GSD3XY3EVQH0JJRED") { r_7A4AY51TXG87NVHR9J1XNZTJQ9
Develop connected knowledge for understanding, investigation, making, maintenance and preservation. The subject entrances below are the curriculum itself; there is no separate numbered inventory.

**Structure.** Keep one descriptively named entrance Record per subject under `institute/trails/`. Put its scope in that Record and connect it to its broader branch with `contains` assertions. An entrance may begin with only its description; `outline` means its formation is unfinished. Reuse an existing entrance and its identity instead of maintaining a second planning Record. Shared knowledge may serve several branches.

**Order.** Develop breadth first: shared area foundations across the tree, then major branches across those areas, then specializations. Hephaestus has mathematics, physics, chemistry, computing, engineering and scientific inquiry. Astronomy belongs within physics; productive infrastructure belongs within engineering; clean manufacturing belongs within production engineering. Pure theory retains its scope alongside practical applications. Deep existing material can supply a bounded prerequisite without becoming a compulsory detour.

**Formation.** Start accessibly and introduce notation and assumptions where used. Progress through substantial reading, connected explanations, worked examples, practice, advanced theory, independent investigation, criticism and revision. Divide large readings into explicit sections. Match evidence to the subject and the claimed depth; descriptions, file counts and related completed subjects do not complete a trail. For practical systems, connect inputs, skills, materials, energy, equipment, transport, losses, maintenance, recovery and cooperation.

**Sources.** Inspect primary sources and record authors, editions, language, actual passages, availability, attribution and reuse terms. Distinguish inspected selections from larger assignments, and original calculations from reproduced published results or physical experiments. Prefer open, preservable sources; keep PDFs, EPUBs, datasets and other source media external to this repository. Preserve source identities and references.

**Connections.** Use ordinary Records and meaningful assertions. Imports provide discovery; directories do not establish learning order. Open this map's branches separately; the map links the curriculum without importing every source into one publication. A Protein selects the endpoints and connections of matching predicates; contextual links do not automatically join that selection. Publish predicate meanings with the content. Do not add reverse assertions merely to display incoming links. Retrieval does not enact actions. No separate Trail feature, manifest or personal operational data is required.

**Verification and continuity.** Check syntax, identities, targets, selected routes and reachability, discovery, export and relocated reopening. Independently check calculations and preserve reused material. Distinguish authored, locally checked, published and learner-demonstrated work. Keep unfinished scope and the next breadth-first step with the trail; record detailed evidence separately in development Records. Update those Records after each completed block; do not recreate Markdown inventories or delete an entrance when it is developed.

**Sensitive material.** Assess explanations, exercises and combined source selections for harmful operational detail. Preserve safe scientific context and use benign models or published observations where appropriate. A reported sensitive stop remains **TODO — sensitive data** on the affected trail, with its reason and safe remaining scope; do not repeatedly retry it or bypass the limit through links. Completion never requires dangerous experimentation.


**Branches:**

- [Ergon — useful labor and productive knowledge](../ergon/Ergon.lingua#r_FE78A5A2D2A3261F711703DCC1)
- [Scholazein — pursuits of a well-spent life](../scholazein/Scholazein.lingua#r_E8E2D1B2D2994E0AD5F5D002D6)
- [Ascholia — bureaucracy and administration](../ascholia/Ascholia.lingua#r_C13F57992B4DED1C03FB1AF28D)
- [Lince — using and understanding the ecosystem](Lince-trails.lingua#r_5CC329E69581876107C84531CE)
- [First connected pathways](../pathways/First-connected-pathways.lingua#r_3RYVEGQ60GSD3XY3EVQH0JJRED)

**Current development.** The curriculum now lives in the connected subject entrances. An outline is an unfinished entrance, not a completed course. Continue development breadth first using the guidance above.

The six Hephaestus common foundations have 637 learning Records, selected with six maps and the root as 644 Records. The first mathematics middle-layer opening has ten lessons and its entrance. Full subject formation remains unfinished. Existing completed subjects and their evidence are preserved; their historical inventory ratio is not a percentage of civilization reproduced.

Next substantive work is the classical-mechanics branch, followed by comparable chemistry, computing, engineering and inquiry blocks. Reuse generalized-coordinate, virtual-work, Lagrange and Hamiltonian material already present; derive a coherent Newton-to-Lagrange bridge and independently check constraint reactions and work. A moving-guide example may expose the distinction between zero virtual work and actual reaction power. Inspect existing studies and actual primary passages before choosing it. Keep full specialist mechanics for later passes.

Clean manufacturing remains under production engineering. Its continuation is `cm-qualification-review`; semiconductor/precision, optical/space, continuing-operation and final research work remain unfinished. Preserve the specific microbial-method **TODO — sensitive data** in that trail.

Before this migration, the mathematics opening passed 12,632 extracted-program assertions, parser and warnings-as-errors Cargo. Publication/export/relocation for spacetime, astronomy and that opening was still pending. The older magnetic verification uses immutable snapshot `/tmp/hephaestus-magnetic-pass-verification/`, manifest `/tmp/hephaestus-magnetic-pass-snapshot.json` (3,917 hashes), runtime handle 54055 and scope 618 selected / 2,888 discovered. Check its actual terminal result and hashes before recording success; it cannot validate this new skeleton. Earlier temporary generators assume the removed register layout and must not be rerun over this migration.

Historical app checks also included source/Sync views, keyboard link navigation, incoming-link display, opening/return and workspace restoration; prior unrelated interface compilation failures were not evidence of content failure. Recheck relevant application behavior when publishing or changing the interface. No interface feature is introduced by this content migration.

The skeleton migration mapped 261 former scope entries into 242 new entrances and 19 existing entrances, with an additional Art entrance for its previously stated scope. All 225 specialist scope descriptions and existing learning routes were preserved. Hephaestus now discovers 3,752 documents through imports; its common selection remains 644 Records. Structural checks found no broken local links or orphan outlines. The Hephaestus parser passed; the whole-tree checker retained the same 1,398 pre-existing diagnostics, with none introduced. Both focused Rust tests passed using the existing compiled publication library: connected hierarchy and outline export/relocation. Warnings-as-errors Cargo check and Cargo test remain pending behind another workspace build; the full Hephaestus export/relocation test has not been completed for this migration.

**Evidence:** [Ergon history](../development/Ergon-development-history.lingua#r_004BC03BE0BE88A0F234F0917F); [Hephaestus history](../development/Hephaestus-development-history.lingua#r_004F2D2D6522AAD1B4563F57DE).
